+
+## Parameter storage and CopyEvent (proposed; not executed)
+
+Candidate-only changes for commit `b7d0cb6a79fe196657deb9711647f8486bcc5e5e`:
+SetEventParameter, GetEventParameter, RemoveEventParameter and CopyEvent.
+Event nodes and payloads use the event's original CFAllocatorRef; replacements
+acquire the new value before releasing the old. Cloning rolls back on any
+allocation error. CopyEvent directly allocates through the original allocator,
+without invoking CreateEvent's clock-dependent zero-time path. Retained
+CoreFoundation pointers and typeEventRef are released
+with their respective APIs. Access to an event's parameter list, including
+CopyEvent, must be externally serialized; retain/release counts stay atomic.
+
+`parameters.c` adds proposed, non-executed regression cases for buffer bounds,
+zero-size payloads, replacement, original/copy independence, retain/release,
+allocation failures at successive clone stages, and allocator preservation.
+It uses the test-only allocator adapter, NOT the real CoreFoundation runtime.
+Apple documents type coercion through AppleEvent handlers, but this candidate
+does not implement it: only the original type and typeWildCard are accepted.
+The chosen errAECoercionFail and errAEBufferTooSmall results and the short-buffer
+no-write behavior are not claimed to be proven Mac OS X equivalence.
+This candidate has NOT qualified the complete historical retention matrix,
+including typeHIAccessibleObjectRef, whose numeric type code was not established.
+The test adapter proves no real MenuRef, HIShapeRef or CF object behavior.
+CopyEvent retains nested typeEventRef objects; it does not recursively copy them.
+Reference cycles must be broken by callers before final release.
+CFIndex/ByteCount sizes and exported ABI require i386 plus real runtime checks.
+The previous 54 checks are historical and do not qualify these changes.
